# Classified `unread-state` findings, as of 2026-08-10.
#
# Every line without a leading `#` is a field the client stores and never reads,
# which has been triaged. The comments ARE the audit: a hit with no rationale
# above it has not been classified, and the audit has not passed.
#
# Lines beginning `# OPEN:` are reprinted on every run. Use them for hits that
# are correctly classified and still wrong — a green exit means "nothing new",
# never "nothing wrong".
#
# --- The one real bug -----------------------------------------------------
#
# OPEN: Common.spirit_spheres — ZC_SPIRITS is modelled, registered, evented,
# OPEN:   routed and stored, and NOTHING DRAWS IT. Monk spirit spheres and
# OPEN:   Gunslinger coins have never rendered. The `spirit-spheres` headless
# OPEN:   scenario is green because it asserts the wire; `event-routing.py` is
# OPEN:   green because the arm stores a value. This is the fifth recorded
# OPEN:   instance of "the data arrives and nothing displays it".
# OPEN:   It is also absent from `EntityData`, so an `AddEntity` rebuild wipes
# OPEN:   it with nothing to re-send — but fixing that changes nothing visible
# OPEN:   until something renders the spheres. Needs a live pass, not a
# OPEN:   headless one. See tools/audits/observer-parity.baseline (A2).
Common.spirit_spheres
#
# --- Deserialisation targets: the field models a FILE FORMAT ---------------
#
# why: these structs exist to parse a document, and a field is present because
# the document has it, not because anything consumes it. Deleting them would
# break the parse or silently drop data we may want later. This is the largest
# and dullest category, and it is why the audit needs a baseline at all.
#
# `clientinfo.xml` — the official client's service descriptor. We read the
# server list and little else; the rest is faithfully parsed and ignored.
ClientInfo.extended_slot
ClientInfo.hide_account_list
ClientInfo.password_encrypt
ClientInfo.password_encrypt2
ClientInfo.read_folder
Service.balloon
Service.game_master_accounts
Service.game_master_yellow_ids
Service.language_type
Service.loading_images
Service.registration_web
#
# Map sky configuration. Sky/cloud rendering is not implemented — these are the
# parsed recipe waiting for it. **If sky rendering ever lands and these are
# still here, that is a bug, not a baseline entry.**
CloudEffect.alpha_dec_speed
CloudEffect.alpha_dec_time
CloudEffect.alpha_dec_time_extra
CloudEffect.alpha_inc_speed
CloudEffect.alpha_inc_time
CloudEffect.alpha_inc_time_extra
CloudEffect.cull_dist
CloudEffect.expand_rate
CloudEffect.height_extra
CloudEffect.num
CloudEffect.size_extra
MapSkyData.bg_color
MapSkyData.bg_fog
MapSkyData.old_cloud_effect
MapSkyData.star_effect
#
# DM data assets (`bestiary.json`, `items.json`, `cards.json`, see
# docs/DM_DATA_GUIDE.md). Exported wholesale from the server databases; the DM
# windows read a subset. `aegis_name` is the server-side identifier, kept so an
# export can be traced back to `item_db.conf`.
BestiaryMonster.chase_range
BestiaryMonster.drops_count
BestiaryMonster.view_range
DmCard.aegis_name
DmItem.aegis_name
#
# --- Reflected by a derive, not read by hand -------------------------------
#
# why: `#[derive(RustState, StateElement)]` renders these through the state
# system, which reflects over the fields. There is no `.field` and no bare
# identifier because the generated code does not spell them out. The audit
# cannot see that, and rather than teach it to parse derives, the shape is
# recorded here.
#
# The debug cache window (`ToggleCacheStatisticsWindow`) displays all eight.
CacheStatistics.action_cache
CacheStatistics.animation_cache
CacheStatistics.effect_cache
CacheStatistics.font_cache
CacheStatistics.map_cache
CacheStatistics.sound_cache
CacheStatistics.sprite_cache
CacheStatistics.texture_cache
#
# Stored when a trade opens. Nothing needs the partner's id yet — the window
# keys off the name — but it is the field any "is this still the same partner"
# check would use, and the trade scenarios have already been bitten once by
# stale partner state.
TradeState.partner_character_id
#
# --- Held to keep something alive ------------------------------------------
#
# why: an RAII handle. It is never read BY DESIGN; dropping it frees the GPU
# resource. The leading underscore is the convention that says so.
StorageTexture._texture
